This image is an elevator safety notice poster issued by "China World Trade Center Property Management". The poster is white-based overall, with deep-red decorative blocks at top and bottom and a clean, standardized layout.
In the top area's upper-left corner is the red-and-black "China World Trade Center Property Management" logo and name. In the middle-right area is the elevator's basic info: on the left an instruction icon in white-on-blue (up-and-down arrows above, three human figures below), and on the right large bold black lettering "Passenger Elevator No. 3, High Zone, Tower 11A", with the ID number "11A-GT-3" below it and, at the very bottom, the note "Served floors: -1, 1~3, 6, 30, 31, 33~43".
Front and center on the poster is the eye-catching big black main title: "Elevator Safety Notice".
Below the title, a two-row, two-column grid shows four icons marked with red prohibition symbols (circle plus slash), each captioned bilingually in Chinese and English:
Upper-left icon: inside the sign, the elevator car packed with people; the text below reads "Overloading is forbidden" and "No overloading".
Upper-right icon: inside the sign, two hands trying to pry open barred elevator doors; the text below reads "Prying the doors open is forbidden" and "Opening door by hand in not permitted".
Lower-left icon: inside the sign, a person standing in the middle of the elevator doors blocking them from closing; the text below reads "Blocking the door is forbidden" and "Do not block the door".
Lower-right icon: inside the sign, a person leaning against the elevator door; the text below reads "Leaning is forbidden" and "No leaning".
The poster's lower half is a two-column list using black diamond bullets (◆) spelling out detailed, text-version safety precautions:
Left column:
◆ Do not take the elevator during a fire;
◆ Do not jump or roughhouse inside the elevator;
◆ Do not manually block the elevator doors from closing;
◆ Carrying flammable, explosive items or hazardous chemicals into the elevator is forbidden;
Right column:
◆ Forcing the elevator doors open is forbidden;
◆ Removing or damaging the elevator's signage is forbidden;
◆ Running the elevator while faulty is forbidden;
◆ Use of the elevator's triangle key by non-professionals is forbidden.
In the bottom-right corner of the deep-red block at the very bottom of the poster is a white corporate slogan: "Born of sincerity · Perfected to perfection".

